6b1318071dae3ca6d5.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":10,"type":"MSQ","correct":"A,C,D","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>Consider the following grammar:</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/6eb7857298b525840b817f12a4fcef0a38f75a8c.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n<div>Which of the following is/are viable prefixes?</div>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> @SaaA</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> aa*+</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> aaA+b</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> aaS*</div>","isCorrect":true}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(a, c, d)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/498b6fedefdbd7afdcce53d1372da3d9230d74f2.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":11,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>The number of states in CLR(1) parsing table for the following grammar is ________.</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/a8c1260163b3f4c450acc7055550844577cf573d.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"12","high":"12"},"solution":"<p>12</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/bba075a04783370a99e26b23422dc9077e287d54.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":12,"type":"MCQ","correct":"B","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>Following is the given syntax directed translation:</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/df7a5343d6f461e0597cc7dca007c0c9b44efa79.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n<div>Find out the abstract syntax tree structure for the following input to the SDT?<br />\nInput → 2 * 3 + 4/5</div>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/8675c1e564a352c080df088fb27ac903f8c84832.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/eb048251e760da525727a0d617bb14a8e51ce29f.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/5318c3f04e177090e24564509755cae71eac976c.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/b0e85681a4fa2ce57f323b3fbbe4052145e28363.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/4dcb6fd9ec25ee19570d3e9ebdf49e33fc5f44f8.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":13,"type":"MSQ","correct":"A,D","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>Which of the following statement(s) are true about lexical analysis in a compiler?</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> It uses regular expressions to define the patterns of valid tokens.</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> It detects syntax error in source code.</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> It eliminates white space and expand macros in the source code.</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> It convert code into meaningful sequence of characters.</div>","isCorrect":true}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(a, d)<br />\n(a) Token pattern are defined using regular expressions.<br />\n(b) Syntactic errors are handled in the syntax analysis phase not by the lexical phase.<br />\n(c) Lexer removes white space but macro expansion done by preprocessor.<br />\n(d) Lexical analysis turns the character stream into meaning tokens (line = int, a = etc.).</p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":14,"type":"MCQ","correct":"B","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>Consider the following syntax directed definition:</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/4e29edd4e96efeacc7fd8ef16620ced5bfa56e30.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n<div>Select the correct option among the following.</div>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> The above SDD is S-attributed.</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> The above SSD is L-attributed.</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> The above SDD is neither S-attributed nor L-attributed.</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> The above SDD is both S-attributed and L-attributed.</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/d24f0f097e736423c06bab7481477af5670fad9b.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":15,"type":"MCQ","correct":"D","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>Which of the following is the correct representation for the following intermediate code in static assignment.</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/9ea5bd8bf0f649c79256687e21c8b030cd83ef8b.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/64138add8834ca35ef0f92b68fe46d567519c9c5.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/c73579463ec3c6c69133f61b90888d3b1009bab5.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/e53115d382d6e56559960c78c243e6d4b64a9121.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/a40990d84010c310129049b5b5f475aa785d9194.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":true}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(d)<br />\nSSA operation: LHS variable should be unique.<br />\nNo optimization in 3-address code.</p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":16,"type":"MCQ","correct":"A","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>Consider the following statements about a basic block in a compiler:<br />\n<em>S</em><sub>1</sub> : A basic block contains no conditional or unconditional jump instruction.<br />\n<em>S</em><sub>2</sub> : A basic block may have multiple entry points but only one exit point.<br />\n<em>S</em><sub>3</sub> : A basic block is a sequence of instruction with only one entry and one exit point.<br />\nWhich of the following is correct?</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <em>S</em><sub>3</sub> only</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <em>S</em><sub>1</sub> and <em>S</em><sub>2</sub> only</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <em>S</em><sub>2</sub> only</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> All are true</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(a)<br />\n<em>S</em><sub>1</sub> : False: Because a basic block can contain jumps. It just can&rsquo;t have jumps into the middle of it.<br />\n<em>S</em><sub>2</sub> : False: A basic block has only one entry and exit point and no branches except at the end.<br />\n<em>S</em><sub>3</sub> : True: Standard definition of basic block.</p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":17,"type":"MCQ","correct":"A","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>Consider the following 3-address code:</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/efba7f093f2d33fcad29915938852d26bc764416.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n<div>Which of the following is true about Control Flow Graph (CFG) of the above code segment<br />\n(excluding start and end nodes).</div>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> CFG has 4 leaders and 4 edges.</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> CFG has 5 leaders and 5 edges.</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> CFG has on basis block, having no entry point.</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> None of these</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(a)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/aed789c42c18debe96402448a9c9071a798ee421.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n<div> </div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":18,"type":"MSQ","correct":"A,C","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>Consider the following C code segment:</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/3085704e6d87eb115abbc37eebcaa8fe206ccb58.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n<div>Which of the following is/are true for above code, when no memory spills is present.</div>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> Code require 7 registers without optimization.</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> Code require 6 registers with code motion optimization.</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> Code require 7 registers with common sub expression elimination optimization.</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> Code has loop invariant, common sub expressions and dead code elimination possibility.</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(a, c)</p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":19,"type":"MCQ","correct":"B","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>Consider the following C code segment:</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/8bb3f63af8a75f321b43c77a30f26be5784cb0d0.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n<div>Which one of the following variables at the exit point of line 4 by block analysis.</div>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/4355b84f9343661a7b4bde54f509be7e8664db22.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/d5e50dd4f4b6be21428ba773eb2f47473ca074ee.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/fbb26512050d88db4f68a847dd6f420a7874a243.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/6036147ce482f392bee762107530c2bc78ef4194.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":20,"type":"MCQ","correct":"A","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>Consider the following intermediate code fragment:</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/803eef361ffc5b09382d107c3b93e15fd4d427e0.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n<div>Consider the following statements:<br />\n<em>S</em><sub>1</sub> : Redundant code elimination can be applied between line 1 and line 2.<br />\n<em>S</em><sub>2</sub> : Algebraic simplification can be used to eliminate line 3 and line 4.<br />\n<em>S</em><sub>3</sub> : Copy propagation can be applied in line 8 after line 7.<br />\nWhich of the following code o